8. STUDY ORGANIZATION

8.1 Sponsor

The trial is sponsored by Meridian Therapeutics Pte. Ltd., with registered offices at 1 Raffles Quay, #18-01, Singapore 048583. All Sponsor obligations under this protocol may be delegated to contract research organizations or other qualified vendors, and such delegations will be documented in writing.

- Ensuring the trial is conducted in accordance with the protocol, Good Clinical Practice (GCP), and applicable regulatory requirements;
- Overseeing the medical care of participants during the trial and ensuring that adequate medical resources are available;
- Ensuring that each participant provides written informed consent prior to any trial-related procedure;
- Maintaining delegation logs and ensuring that all site staff assigned to trial duties are appropriately qualified and trained;
- Ensuring accurate and timely data entry into the electronic Case Report Form (eCRF);
- Reporting adverse events and serious adverse events to the Sponsor and the Institutional Review Board in accordance with Section 10;
- Retaining essential documents as required by GCP and applicable regulations.

The PI may delegate trial-related duties to qualified members of the site staff, provided that the delegation is documented on the Site Delegation Log and signed by both the PI and the delegate. The PI retains ultimate responsibility for all delegated tasks.

8.3 Sub-investigator

Dr. Marcus Tan's role_in_protocol is Sub-investigator. Record status: current.

The Sub-investigator will perform trial-related procedures under the supervision of the PI, including participant screening, eligibility assessments, physical examinations, adverse event assessments, and other duties as assigned and documented on the Site Delegation Log. The Sub-investigator will also participate in protocol training and site initiation visits as required.

8.4 Study Coordinator

A qualified study coordinator will be assigned to manage day-to-day trial activities at the site. Responsibilities include:

- Scheduling participant visits and coordinating study procedures;
- Preparing and maintaining the Investigator Site File (ISF);
- Facilitating communication between the site, the Sponsor, and the CIRB;
- Assisting with data entry and query resolution;
- Coordinating the collection, processing, and shipment of laboratory samples in accordance with the Laboratory Manual.

8.5 Other Site Staff

Additional site staff may be assigned to specific trial duties, including research assistants, nurses, and pharmacy staff. All staff involved in the trial will be listed on the Site Delegation Log with their respective duties, and will receive protocol-specific training prior to performing any trial-related activity. Training records will be maintained in the ISF.

8.6 Sponsor Responsibilities

The Sponsor is responsible for:

- Obtaining regulatory approval or clearance for the trial in Singapore;
- Providing the investigational product (PT-101) and ensuring its quality and stability;
- Monitoring the trial in accordance with the Monitoring Plan;
- Collecting, reviewing, and analyzing trial data;
- Reporting suspected unexpected serious adverse reactions (SUSARs) to the Health Sciences Authority (HSA) and the CIRB;
- Providing insurance coverage or indemnification for trial-related injury as required by applicable regulations.

8.7 Data Safety Monitoring Board

An independent Data Safety Monitoring Board (DSMB) will be convened to review safety data at specified intervals. The DSMB will comprise at least three members with relevant expertise, including at least one clinician with experience in metabolic disorders. The DSMB will provide recommendations to the Sponsor regarding trial continuation, modification, or termination based on its review of unblinded safety data. Further details are provided in the DSMB Charter.

8.8 Financial Disclosure

The PI and Sub-investigator will provide current financial disclosure information to the Sponsor prior to trial initiation and will update this information during the trial and for one year following trial completion, in accordance with applicable regulations.
